# k10draw — the draw donor venue config (15-05, USPACE-08, D-04).
#
# The kernel-local devdraw venue: k10t1's header discipline + device set,
# PLUS k10f's draw deltas (k10f:25-28,39-40,193-199) with the BIOS-VBE
# route REPLACED by the qemu-native DISPI VGAdev (route 1, 15-RESEARCH
# Pattern 4): the venue boots text-mode under `qemu -kernel ... -vga std`,
# userspace drives the mode-set through #v/vgactl (`type dispi`,
# `linear`, `size 1024x768x32 x8r8g8b8`, `drawinit` — devvga.c's
# CMsize/CMdrawinit verbs), the LFB maps through the in-tree
# vgalinearpci(), and /dev/draw/new opens against the kernel-local
# devdraw (#i).  The vesa VGAdev and the real-mode trampoline link are
# deliberately ABSENT (k10 serves no BIOS-call service — Enonexist,
# Pitfall 1), as is any sd section (k10t1 carries none).
#
# The device/dbgflg/mach/port/dir sections are k10t1's set VERBATIM
# (its header rule: DO NOT PRUNE) — the deliberate deltas vs k10t1 are
# ONLY:
#   dev     — the k10f draw device set appended (draw/mouse/vga/kbmap)
#   vga     — the NEW `vga +dev` section naming vgadispi (k10/vgadispi.c,
#             the 9k/386 vesa VGAdev's struct shape with DISPI for enable)
#   rootdir — the venue embed set below (the draw smoke's minimal boot:
#             rc/echo/cat/test/sleep/read/bind/paqfs + rcmain + the
#             host-built drawsmoke + k10draw.rc as /boot/boot; the
#             -initrd module carries everything else)
#   lib     — k10f's libdraw family ahead of k10cpu's lib set (the kernel
#             links the /amd64/lib archives 15-04's tier-0 closure built)
# k10cpu/k10t1/k10f stay untouched (the frozen-config discipline).

